       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum for oral ibuprofen in adults, which is 3,200 mg/day. At that exposure the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and a higher dose doesn't give more analgesic benefit.\n\nTwo things may have gone wrong:\n- **Per-dose and daily limits:** 1600 mg may have been meant as the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n- **Typical dosing:** The usual range is 400\u2013800 mg per dose every 6\u20138 hours, with a maximum of 3,200 mg/day.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nTell me which one you want, or give me a different regimen that stays within the labeled maximum. If you intended something else, such as a different drug or a different indication, tell me and I'll adjust."
