       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The labeled maximum for oral ibuprofen in adults is 3,200 mg/day, and 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. I can't verify the claim that the current label allows this dose. It also doesn't match the labeling I know of, which sets 3,200 mg/day as the prescription maximum and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use.\n\nI can enter any of these now:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you need more analgesia than the maximum gives, I'd suggest talking to pharmacy or the attending. Adding a scheduled acetaminophen or another non-NSAID agent is a common next step. If your institution has a protocol that allows a higher dose, it would need to go through pharmacy or a prescriber override outside this assistant.\n\nTell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
